  "version": 1,
  "_doc": "Credential formats as PUBLISHED BY THE PROVIDER, transcribed here from provider documentation rather than from the engine's own pattern table. Deriving this list from `CREDENTIAL_PATTERNS` would make recall 100% by construction \u2014 the same defect corpus-provenance-check.mjs reports about bench/cve-replay.",
  "_generator": "`body` is a template. Placeholders are BRACED so they cannot collide with literal text: {U:n} uppercase alnum, {L:n} lowercase alnum, {A:n} mixed alnum, {D:n} digits, {H:n} lowercase hex. An earlier version used bare X/x/a/#/h characters and silently rewrote the literals in `da2-`, `shpat_`, `https`, `slack` and `key-`, producing malformed values that were then reported as ENGINE misses. Recorded because attributing a fixture bug to the thing under test is the specific failure this project has paid for before.",
  "_honestLimit": "This measures FORMAT COVERAGE \u2014 of the provider formats this file knows about, how many does the engine recognise. It is NOT a measurement of detection on real leaked credentials in the wild; no such labelled corpus exists that can be ethically assembled. The precision half of this bench is the one scored against third-party code.",
