  "_context": "Each value is planted as an assignment to a provider-named variable \u2014 `const twilioCredential = \"...\"` \u2014 because several provider formats are only distinguishable WITH nearby context (a bare `SK`+32 hex is not identifiably Twilio), and because that is how a leaked credential actually appears in source.",
  "_headroom": "Formats are added when the instrument saturates. A bench sitting at 100% cannot fail, and a gate that cannot fail measures nothing \u2014 the PRD's governing rule. The eight entries after digitalocean-pat were added for exactly that reason; several are context-dependent shapes (a bare 32-hex string is only identifiably a key because of the variable it is assigned to), which is the honest next difficulty tier rather than more prefixed tokens."
